VisWiz WooCommerce Visualizer
=============================

Version 1.7.5 GitHub Auto Updates

- Added native WordPress update discovery from the latest GitHub Release.
- Added automatic VisWiz plugin updates through the normal WordPress updater.
- Release updates require the installable `viswiz-{version}.zip` asset, preventing unsafe GitHub source-archive upgrades.
- Added release packaging automation for future version bumps on `main`.
- Automatic updates can be disabled with `define('VISWIZ_AUTO_UPDATES', false);` in `wp-config.php`.

Version 1.7.4 Full Info Modal Label Settings

Backend/editor improvements in 1.6.9:
- Removed the redundant mini graph preview from the Nodes editing tab.
- Reorganized global Settings into Overview, Commerce Defaults, Manual Fallback Data, Legacy Diagram Defaults, and Legacy Graph Defaults.
- Added clearer settings cards, explanations, and quick links to the dedicated Visualizations/Datasets/Schema screens.


- Node detail modal now shows a gallery carousel with the featured image first.
- Left/right arrows appear when a node has multiple images.
- Gallery data is exported in the graph payload as ordered image objects while preserving legacy image URL fields.

This build focuses on graph-data entry UX:

- Builder-style admin IA: Dashboard, Visualizations, Datasets, Node Types, Relation Types, Settings.
- Dedicated dataset management and JSON export.
- Canonical node type schema with editable subtypes.
- Relation type schema with label, inverse label, default direction, default intensity, and usual source/target node types/subtypes.
- Node editor improvements:
  - auto-generated readable node IDs from titles,
  - manual node ID editing with relation updates,
  - duplicate node hints,
  - per-node validation status,
  - relation cards grouped into incoming/outgoing relations,
  - quick outgoing/incoming relation creation,
  - create connected node + relation in one flow,
  - save/add-relation and save/add-connected-node actions.
- Relation editor improvements:
  - default direction/intensity from relation type,
  - reverse relation action,
  - relation type mismatch warnings,
  - relation cards in node context.
- Dataset validation panel for missing titles/types/endpoints, duplicates, and relation-schema warnings.
- Quick add drawers for pasted nodes and relations with preflight validation.
- Proposed subtype approval now registers real subtypes into the global Node Types schema.
- Gutenberg block picker, shortcode copy buttons, dirty-change warning, and improved admin polish.

Additional 1.6.1 fixes:

- Rebuilt the visualization editor guide so it updates dynamically by visualization type and data source.
- Removed contradictory guide/manual-section visibility for timeline, flow diagram, and org chart.
- Timeline now consistently uses chart-style type-aware rows; legacy diagram sections are only shown for the legacy Diagram type.
- Flow Diagram and Org Chart now consistently follow the graph workflow: nodes, type usage/proposals, relations, validation, and preview.
- Builder workflow steps now follow the active editor tab instead of remaining stuck on Data source.
- Preview now handles all chart-like types with a generic chart preview instead of only Pie.

This build has been syntax-checked but should be tested on a WordPress staging site before wider use.

Additional 1.6.2 fixes:

- Fixed node autosave so updating a node no longer wipes existing graph relations when the autosave payload contains no meaningful relation data.
- Added safer preservation/remapping of existing relation endpoints during node-only autosaves, including node ID changes.
- Relation modal “Save & close” now uses the graph autosave path.
- Frontend graph node detail modals now render formatted node descriptions as sanitized rich HTML with paragraph/list spacing, instead of falling back to flat/plain text.


Additional 1.6.3 fixes:
- Relation fields that point to existing dataset/schema values now use smart searchable comboboxes while keeping the original select fields for safe saving.
- From/To node fields in standalone relation cards, node inline relation editors, and quick relation creation now search by title, label, and node ID.
- Relation type fields now use the same smart search and show slug, direction, source/target expectations, and description where available.


Additional 1.6.6 fixes:

- Node-only autosave no longer replaces or deletes relations. It preserves existing links and only remaps endpoints when node IDs change.
- Full graph saves now defend against empty/partial relation payloads caused by hidden/modal UI state.
- Replaced fragile wp_editor-in-hidden-details node descriptions with a lightweight HTML-capable description editor and formatting toolbar.
- Public graph detail modals now receive cleaner sanitized rich description HTML and preserve paragraphs, links, lists, emphasis, and blockquotes.
- Fixed admin and public modal layout issues where close buttons could appear outside the visible modal frame.


Keyboard/WYSIWYG improvements in 1.7.0:

Modal deletion fixes in 1.7.1:
- Remove node/relation actions now cleanly close editor modals and remove overlays.
- Deleting a node also removes its attached relations to avoid orphan graph edges.

- Modal-safe WYSIWYG editor for node descriptions, initialized only while the node editor modal is open.
- Keyboard trap and focus restoration for node/relation editing modals.
- Smart searchable relation fields support Arrow Up/Down, Home/End, Enter selection, Escape close.
- Ctrl/Cmd+Enter saves and closes the active node/relation modal.
- Builder tabs support arrow-key navigation.

Additional 1.7.3 fixes:
- Round and compact graph nodes now calculate their own dimensions from the full node title, avoiding title truncation/ellipsis in those node styles.
- Added optional relation-count sizing for graph nodes: round nodes grow by radius and basic info cards grow in width/height according to each node’s number of relations.
- Added global and per-visualization controls for relation-count sizing, per-relation size step, maximum size increase, and the public full screen toggle.
- Added a Full screen / Exit full screen toggle for public progress, chart, diagram, and graph visualizations, with graph re-rendering after entering/exiting full screen so the layout uses the available viewport.

Additional 1.7.4 fixes:
- Added per-visualization full info modal label controls in the Display tab for graph-style visualizations.
- Added matching global display defaults for node modal labels.
- Public graph node modals now use the configured text for related-node headings, relation fallbacks, direction labels, image gallery labels, proposed subtype labels, custom field fallback labels, and type/subtype drill-down headings.
